which multiplies the current value by 2(raised to) INTEGER. (The exponent integer may
be terminated by ' or . to force its radix; otherwise it used the current radix.)
The result is a fixed-point integer! For instance, 1.5 (leftarrow) 3 = 14'; and
17' (leftarrow) 3 = 170'.

